      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Fundamentally: demand curves. The less I have of something, the more valuable it is to me.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Fundamentally: demand curves. The less I have of something, the more valuable it is to me.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "3ba2bc19-1e3a-4aec-93fb-e8d1d25987d3",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "57431096-7e21-4246-b98c-54c416d7f950"
      },
      "created_time": "2022-06-03T06:17:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2022-06-03T06:48:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Let’s say I have 100 blueberries; I’m trying to sell some of them and eat the rest for lunch. My first few blueberries, I can sell pretty cheaply because I wasn’t going to eat them anyways, say for $0.01 each. But after selling 50, I’m running out of blueberries I wanted to sell, so I’d raise the price to $0.02. If someone really likes these and they buy 25 more, I might double the price again to $0.04 on the next blueberry. But my last few blueberries are the most precious to me; I might price my 10th-to-last blueberry at $0.10, and my very last blueberry at $1.00.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Let’s say I have 100 blueberries; I’m trying to sell some of them and eat the rest for lunch. My first few blueberries, I can sell pretty cheaply because I wasn’t going to eat them anyways, say for $0.01 each. But after selling 50, I’m running out of blueberries I wanted to sell, so I’d raise the price to $0.02. If someone really likes these and they buy 25 more, I might double the price again to $0.04 on the next blueberry. But my last few blueberries are the most precious to me; I might price my 10th-to-last blueberry at $0.10, and my very last blueberry at $1.00.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
